 "notes": "Stochastic 95% CL upper limit on g_phi_gamma from Fig. 5 (solid red, 'POLARBEAR (this work)'), assuming the axion is all of the dark matter with rho0=0.3 GeV/cm^3 and a Rayleigh-distributed local field amplitude (Sec. VI, Eqs. 24-28). Curve extracted from the vector paths of coupling_constraints.pdf in the e-print; axes calibrated from major tick marks and verified against the median line, which reproduces Eq. 28 [g < 2.4e-11 GeV^-1 (m/1e-21 eV)] to ~1%. The plotted exact bound oscillates rapidly with frequency (515 frequencies, 0.67x-3.1x the median); reported points are per-log-bin medians of that curve (80 bins), which track the paper's quoted median limit. Mass range 9.6e-22 to 2.2e-20 eV (Eq. 30). The stochastic-field limit is the paper's headline result; the deterministic median (Eq. 25, 1.1e-11 GeV^-1 x m/1e-21 eV, dashed) is 2.2x stronger and not reported.",
